## UI
item.utilitycraft:absolute_drill=Absolute Drill\n§7- Mines in a 7x7 area\n§o§9@UC: Ascendant Technology
ui.utilitycraft:info.power_beacon=Stores Dorios Energy received from a connected energy network and distributes it wirelessly to compatible machines inside its tier range. Transfer is shared fairly between receivers that currently have free capacity. Use the power button on the main panel to enable or disable transmission.
ui.utilitycraft:info.laser_barrier=Projects a solid, indestructible energy wall in a straight line from the front of the machine. The base field is 3 blocks long and 3 blocks high. Entities touching or standing very close to the projected wall take contact damage. The barrier never replaces existing blocks, so obstructed cells remain empty and are reported on the status screen.\n\nThe left Size Upgrade slot increases length and the middle Size Upgrade slot increases height, up to eight levels each. The Energy Upgrade slot reduces upkeep. Use the power button to enable or disable the projection. The field shuts down automatically when energy is insufficient.
ui.utilitycraft:info.refining_table=Refines registered StatsCore weapons, tools, and armor. Insert one equipment item and a Chip, then optionally add up to eight supported ingots to improve the quality range. Supply liquid XP and press Refine. Repeating a refinement rerolls the item with progressively higher XP and energy costs.\n\nA Runic Core can awaken a locked unique ability during the roll. Refinement is stored directly on the item and may grant combat, mining, or defensive attributes according to its StatsCore profile. Speed and Energy upgrades affect processing.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Equipment Input§r inserts supported gear.\n§bMaterial Input§r inserts Chips, ingots, and Runic Cores.\n§1Input All§r exposes all inputs.\n§cEquipment Output§r extracts the equipment slot.\n\nLiquid I/O:\n§9XP Input§r fills the liquid XP tank.
ui.utilitycraft:io.refining_table.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Equipment Input\n§r- §bMaterial Input\n§r- §1Input All\n§r- §cEquipment Output
ui.utilitycraft:io.refining_table.liquids=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9XP Input
ui.utilitycraft:info.abyssal_fisher=Uses a Fishing Net and an internal Water tank to gather fishing loot automatically. The installed net defines loot tier, luck, roll count, catch chance, and amount. Every completed cast damages the net, and catches enter the shared 18-slot output buffer. There is one predictable processing mode with no hidden drop modifier, loss, or extra consumption. Speed, Energy, and Hyper Processing upgrades affect the cycle.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Net Input§r accepts Fishing Nets.\n§cOutput§r exposes the complete catch buffer.\n\nLiquid I/O:\n§9Water Input§r fills the internal Water tank.
ui.utilitycraft:io.abyssal_fisher.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Net Input\n§r- §cOutput
ui.utilitycraft:io.abyssal_fisher.liquids=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Water Input
ui.utilitycraft:info.pattern_placer=Places real blocks directly in front of the machine from a pooled 3x3 supply grid. Matching stacks are consumed only for successful placements; occupied cells are never replaced.\n\n1x1: places the central target.\nPlane: places a vertical 3x3 wall.\nCube: fills a 3x3x3 volume.\nLine: places five blocks across the machine face.\n\nThe green button pauses automation. A Wrench toggles the exact placement outline. Speed, Energy, and Hyper Processing upgrades are accepted.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Block Input§r exposes all nine supply slots.
ui.utilitycraft:io.pattern_placer.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Block Input
ui.utilitycraft:info.seismic_breaker=Breaks blocks directly in front of the machine and resolves loot with the optional reusable tool in the cyan slot. Drops enter the 3x3 output buffer; air, liquids, and protected blocks are ignored.\n\n1x1: breaks the central target.\nPlane: breaks a vertical 3x3 wall.\nCube: breaks a 3x3x3 volume.\nLine: breaks five blocks across the machine face.\n\nThe green button pauses automation. A Wrench toggles the working-area outline. Speed, Energy, and Hyper Processing upgrades are accepted.\n\nItem I/O:\n§bTool Input§r accepts a mining tool and preserves it while using its loot behavior.\n§cOutput§r exposes all nine drop slots.
ui.utilitycraft:io.seismic_breaker.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §bTool Input\n§r- §cOutput
ui.utilitycraft:info.verdant_cultivator=Manages a crop field directly in front of the machine. Four seed slots form a repeating 2x2 planting pattern; mature crops are harvested and replanted automatically. The base field is 3x3 and Range upgrades expand it through 11x11.\n\nAccelerator Clock: applies basic growth pulses.\nDiamond Accelerator Clock: doubles the pulse throughput and cycle speed.\nNether Star Accelerator Clock: quadruples throughput and speed, with a chance to advance a second growth stage.\n\nA Wrench toggles the working outline. Collected drops use a 5x3 output buffer with corrected side automation.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Seed Input§r exposes the four pattern slots.\n§bClock Input§r accepts all three accelerator clocks.\n§1Input All§r exposes seeds and the clock.\n§cOutput§r exposes all fifteen harvest slots.
ui.utilitycraft:io.verdant_cultivator.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Seed Input\n§r- §bClock Input\n§r- §1Input All\n§r- §cOutput
ui.utilitycraft:info.genetic_seed_synthesizer=Runs one linear synthesis profile for up to two reusable seed or sapling templates. The soil catalyst is also preserved, and generated drops enter the 15-slot output buffer. Any registered coolant is accepted. Its efficiency divides coolant consumption and multiplies processing speed. Speed, Energy, Hyper Processing, and Process Batch upgrades are accepted.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Seed Input§r exposes both template slots.\n§bSoil Input§r exposes the soil catalyst.\n§1Input All§r exposes seeds and soil.\n§cOutput§r exposes the complete output buffer.\n\nLiquid I/O:\n§9Coolant Input§r accepts registered UtilityCraft coolants.
ui.utilitycraft:io.genetic_seed_synthesizer.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Seed Input\n§r- §bSoil Input\n§r- §1Input All\n§r- §cOutput
ui.utilitycraft:io.genetic_seed_synthesizer.liquids=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Coolant Input
ui.utilitycraft:info.duplicator=Duplicates most items while preserving compatible names, lore, durability, enchantments, and item data. Insert one template and supply Liquified Aetherium. When processing finishes, the original is returned in the upper output and one identical copy appears below it.\n\nItems reserved for the Singularity Fabricator, Lucky Tools, Banners, Potions, and Shulker Boxes are rejected. Every identifier is classified once and then cached. Explicit and pattern-based rarity determine processing time and energy cost; unknown addon items use the normal Common profile. Speed and Energy upgrades affect processing.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Template Input§r accepts duplicable items.\n§cOriginal Output§r returns the consumed template.\n§cCopy Output§r exposes the duplicate.\n§cOutput All§r exposes both outputs.\n\nLiquid I/O:\n§9Aetherium Input§r fills the dedicated Liquified Aetherium tank.
ui.utilitycraft:io.duplicator.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Template Input\n§r- §cOriginal Output\n§r- §cCopy Output\n§r- §cOutput All
ui.utilitycraft:io.duplicator.liquids=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Aetherium Input
ui.utilitycraft:info.singularity_fabricator=Replicates a fixed set of rare materials. Insert one supported template and supply the internal tank with Dark Matter. When processing finishes, the original template is returned in the upper output and one identical copy appears in the lower output. Custom names, lore, and compatible item data are preserved when the output item matches the template.\n\nEach input resolves directly through an indexed recipe. Rarity controls total energy cost; every recipe also defines its own time and Dark Matter cost. Speed and Energy upgrades affect processing.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Template Input§r accepts supported materials.\n§cOriginal Output§r returns the consumed template.\n§cCopy Output§r exposes the replicated item.\n§cOutput All§r exposes both outputs.\n\nLiquid I/O:\n§9Dark Matter Input§r fills the dedicated tank.
ui.utilitycraft:io.singularity_fabricator.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Template Input\n§r- §cOriginal Output\n§r- §cCopy Output\n§r- §cOutput All
ui.utilitycraft:io.singularity_fabricator.liquids=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Dark Matter Input
ui.utilitycraft:info.reinforcement_anvil=Processes one damageable item automatically in its blue shared slot. Every available operation runs in the same cycle: Repair restores 25% of maximum durability, while a valid Tier I, II, or III Reinforcement Module also fills the automatic repair reserve to 25%, 50%, or 100%. With no module, the anvil repairs only. The module is reusable and is never consumed.\n\nReinforced tools and armor spend one reserve point per durability point restored while in use. Run the item again to refill a spent reserve or raise it with a stronger module. The processed item remains in the same blue slot. Speed, Energy, and Hyper Processing upgrades affect processing.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Item Input§r inserts one damageable item into the shared slot.\n§bModule Input§r accepts Reinforcement Modules.\n§1Input All§r exposes both inputs.\n§cProcessed Item§r extracts the shared item slot.
ui.utilitycraft:io.reinforcement_anvil.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Item Input\n§r- §bModule Input\n§r- §1Input All\n§r- §cProcessed Item
entity.utilitycraft:reinforcement_anvil.name=Reinforcement Anvil
tile.utilitycraft:reinforcement_anvil.name=Reinforcement Anvil\n§7Accepts upgrades:\n  §a§r, §b§r, §d§r\n§o§9@UC: Ascendant Technology
ui.utilitycraft:info.enchantment_station=Runs up to nine enchantment operations in parallel. Put target items in the main grid and Enchantability Modules in the three orange slots; completed items remain in their grid slots. The alternate mode can extract enchantments into Books or absorb all enchantments as XP fluid. Refined Aetherium is used as the extraction catalyst.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Main Grid§r inserts targets and can extract their processed versions.\n§bModule Input§r fills the orange module slots.\n§1Disenchant Source§r inserts or extracts the alternate-mode source.\n§bCatalyst Input§r supplies Refined Aetherium.\n§9Book Input§r supplies normal Books.\n§3Input All§r exposes every item input.\n§cProcessed Grid§r, §cProcessed Source§r, and §4Enchanted Books§r expose their respective results.\n§cOutput All§r exposes every item result.\n\nLiquid I/O:\n§9XP Input§r supplies enchanting operations.\n§cXP Output§r drains XP recovered by absorption.\n§9Input §r+ §cOutput§r allows both on one face.
ui.utilitycraft:io.enchantment_station.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Main Grid\n§r- §bModule Input\n§r- §1Disenchant Source\n§r- §bCatalyst Input\n§r- §9Book Input\n§r- §3Input All\n§r- §cProcessed Grid\n§r- §cProcessed Source\n§r- §4Enchanted Books\n§r- §cOutput All
ui.utilitycraft:io.enchantment_station.liquids=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9XP Input\n§r- §cXP Output\n§r- §9Input §r+ §cOutput
ui.utilitycraft:info.arcane_enchanter=Enchants one item at a time. Every applied enchantment costs 12 Lapis Lazuli and 300 mB of XP. Enchantability Modules increase selection strength; the reusable Curse Protection Module prevents curses from entering the generated plan. Speed, Energy, and Hyper Processing upgrades are accepted.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Item Input§r accepts the target item.\n§bLapis Input§r accepts Lapis Lazuli.\n§1Enchantability Module§r raises enchantment strength.\n§3Curse Protection§r filters curses.\n§cOutput§r exposes the enchanted item.\n\nLiquid I/O:\n§9XP Input§r fills the internal XP tank.
ui.utilitycraft:io.arcane_enchanter.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Item Input\n§r- §bLapis Input\n§r- §1Module Input\n§r- §3Input All\n§r- §cOutput
ui.utilitycraft:io.arcane_enchanter.liquids=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9XP Input
ui.utilitycraft:info.disenchanter=Processes one enchanted item in two selectable modes.\n\nExtraction: removes one enchantment, consumes one normal Book, and places the enchanted Book in the 4x3 output grid while leaving the updated source in its large shared slot.\nAbsorption: removes every enchantment and stores the recovered value as XP fluid.\n\nSpeed, Energy, and Hyper Processing upgrades are accepted.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Source Input§r inserts or extracts the enchanted item.\n§bBook Input§r inserts normal Books.\n§cEnchanted Books§r exposes all twelve book outputs.\n\nLiquid I/O:\n§cXP Output§r drains recovered XP.
ui.utilitycraft:io.disenchanter.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Source Input\n§r- §bBook Input\n§r- §3Input All\n§r- §cProcessed Item\n§r- §cEnchanted Book\n§r- §cOutput All
ui.utilitycraft:io.disenchanter.liquids=I/O Modes:\n§r- §cXP Output
ui.utilitycraft:info.industrial_crucible=Processes supported materials while generating Lava. Its six inputs form a 2x3 pooled grid and solid results use a 2x3 output grid. Cobblestone becomes Stone, Sand becomes Glass, and Clay Balls become Bricks. Processing pauses when the solid buffer or Lava tank is full. Speed, Energy, Hyper Processing, and Process Batch upgrades are accepted.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Input Grid§r exposes all six material slots.\n§cOutput Grid§r exposes all six result slots.\n\nLiquid I/O:\n§cLava Output§r exposes the generated Lava tank.
ui.utilitycraft:io.industrial_crucible.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Input Grid\n§r- §cOutput Grid
ui.utilitycraft:io.industrial_crucible.liquids=I/O Modes:\n§r- §cLava Output
ui.utilitycraft:info.cryofluid_synthesizer=Runs one linear recipe that combines weighted Titanium inputs, weighted Lapis inputs, and 1,000 mB Water into 1,000 mB Cryofluid for 6,000 DE. The recipe configuration accepts Titanium, plates, raw Titanium, dust, chunks, nuggets, Lapis Lazuli, and Lapis Blocks at their configured values. Speed, Energy, Hyper Processing, and Process Batch upgrades are accepted.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Titanium Input§r exposes four weighted input slots.\n§bLapis Input§r exposes four weighted input slots.\n\nLiquid I/O:\n§9Water Input§r fills the Water tank.\n§cCryofluid Output§r drains the Cryofluid tank.
ui.utilitycraft:io.cryofluid_synthesizer.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Titanium Input\n§r- §bLapis Input\n§r- §9Input All
ui.utilitycraft:io.cryofluid_synthesizer.liquids=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Water Input\n§r- §cCryofluid Output
ui.utilitycraft:info.cryo_stabilizer=Consumes Cryofluid to stabilize up to four materials simultaneously. Each of the four input lanes writes to its paired output. Capsule insertion, capsule return, and the obsolete unstable-material guide were removed; Cryofluid enters through liquid I/O. Speed, Energy, Hyper Processing, and Process Batch upgrades are accepted.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Material Inputs§r expose the four independent lanes.\n§cStabilized Outputs§r expose all four paired results.\n\nLiquid I/O:\n§9Cryofluid Input§r fills the internal tank.
ui.utilitycraft:io.cryo_stabilizer.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Material Inputs\n§r- §cStabilized Outputs
ui.utilitycraft:io.arc_press_forge.gases=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Steam Input
ui.utilitycraft:io.impact_crusher.gases=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Steam Input
ui.utilitycraft:io.cryo_stabilizer.liquids=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Cryofluid Input
ui.utilitycraft:info.cryo_chamber=Runs three Cryo systems simultaneously. The center Stabilizer converts unstable materials with Cryofluid, the frozen 3x3 grid cools complete stacks, and the generator converts Water, Titanium, and Lapis into Cryofluid.\n\nThe Water and Cryofluid tanks are independent. Speed and Energy upgrades affect the complete machine; Process Batch applies to the Stabilizer and Generator.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Stabilizer Input\n§bCooling Grid\n§1Fluid Containers\n§bTitanium Input\n§9Lapis Input\n§3Input All\n§cStabilized Output\n§cCooling Grid Output\n§cCryofluid Containers\n§cOutput All\n\nLiquid I/O:\n§9Water Input\n§cCryofluid Output
ui.utilitycraft:io.cryo_chamber.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Stabilizer Input\n§r- §bCooling Grid\n§r- §1Fluid Containers\n§r- §bTitanium Input\n§r- §9Lapis Input\n§r- §3Input All\n§r- §cStabilized Output\n§r- §cCooling Grid Output\n§r- §cCryofluid Containers\n§r- §cOutput All
ui.utilitycraft:io.cryo_chamber.liquids=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Water Input\n§r- §cCryofluid Output
ui.utilitycraft:info.cryo_freezer=Freezes up to fifteen stacks simultaneously. Place supported items anywhere in the frozen grid; completed results replace their original stacks in the same slots.\n\nRecipes use direct indexed lookup. The shared coolant tank accepts the liquid required by the active recipe, while all lanes share one energy budget.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Freezer Grid Input\n§cFreezer Grid Output\n\nLiquid I/O:\n§9Coolant Input
ui.utilitycraft:io.cryo_freezer.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Freezer Grid Input\n§r- §cFreezer Grid Output
ui.utilitycraft:io.cryo_freezer.liquids=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Coolant Input
tile.utilitycraft:cryofluid_synthesizer.name=Cryofluid Synthesizer\n§9Superior Cryo Synthesis Branch\n§7- Accepted upgrades:\n  §a§r, §b§r, §d§r, §6§r\n§o§9@UC: Ascendant Technology
entity.utilitycraft:cryofluid_synthesizer.name=§fCryofluid Synthesizer
ui.utilitycraft:info.vaporworks_processor=Converts liquid inputs into pressurized Steam gas. Water produces Steam at a 1:1 ratio; Cryofluid takes longer and produces 50% more Steam. The liquid input tank and Steam gas tank each store 64,000 units.\n\nFilled Water or Cryofluid containers go in the upper-left slot and their empty containers leave below it. Empty gas capsules go in the upper-right slot; a filled 8,000-unit Steam Capsule leaves below it.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Liquid Container Input§r and §bGas Container Input§r accept containers.\n§cContainer Return§r and §cSteam Container Output§r expose processed containers.\n§9Input All§r and §cOutput All§r expose both pairs.\n\nLiquid I/O:\n§9Liquid Input§r accepts Water or Cryofluid.\n\nGas I/O:\n§cSteam Output§r exposes the Steam tank.
ui.utilitycraft:io.vaporworks_processor.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Liquid Container Input\n§r- §bGas Container Input\n§r- §9Input All\n§r- §cContainer Return\n§r- §cSteam Container Output\n§r- §cOutput All
ui.utilitycraft:io.vaporworks_processor.liquids=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Liquid Input
ui.utilitycraft:io.vaporworks_processor.gases=I/O Modes:\n§r- §cSteam Output
ui.utilitycraft:info.energizer=Converts supported iron materials into energized components. Place materials in either input; the Primary channel is checked first, then Auxiliary. Each recipe defines its own processing time and total energy cost.\n\nBoth channels resolve recipes through direct indexed lookup. Speed and Energy upgrades affect processing, while Process Batch controls how many items complete per paid cycle.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Primary Input§r exposes the first-priority channel.\n§bAuxiliary Input§r exposes the fallback channel.\n§9Input All§r exposes both inputs.\n§cOutput§r exposes the result slot.
ui.utilitycraft:io.energizer.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Primary Input\n§r- §bAuxiliary Input\n§r- §9Input All\n§r- §cOutput
ui.utilitycraft:info.catalyst_weaver=Combines one base item with an exact set of up to six catalysts. Catalyst positions do not matter, but extra catalyst types prevent a match. Some recipes also consume Lava, Liquified Aetherium, or Dark Matter from the internal 128,000 mB tank.\n\nCatalyst Weaver recipes and registered UtilityCraft Infuser recipes are indexed when loaded. Recipe lookup does not scan the complete registry while machines run.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Base Input§r exposes the base item.\n§bCatalyst 1§r, §1Catalyst 2§r, §bCatalyst 3§r, §9Catalyst 4§r, §bCatalyst 5§r, and §1Catalyst 6§r each expose one catalyst slot.\n§3Input All§r exposes every item input.\n§cMain Output§r and §cResidue Output§r expose their respective results.\n§cOutput All§r exposes both outputs.\n\nLiquid I/O:\n§9Catalyst Fluid Input§r exposes the internal tank.
ui.utilitycraft:io.catalyst_weaver.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Base Input\n§r- §bCatalyst 1\n§r- §1Catalyst 2\n§r- §bCatalyst 3\n§r- §9Catalyst 4\n§r- §bCatalyst 5\n§r- §1Catalyst 6\n§r- §3Input All\n§r- §cMain Output\n§r- §cResidue Output\n§r- §cOutput All
ui.utilitycraft:io.catalyst_weaver.liquids=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Catalyst Fluid Input
ui.utilitycraft:info.liquifier=Converts supported solid materials into Liquified Aetherium or Dark Matter. Insert the solid material on the left; produced liquid accumulates in the output tank on the right. Some recipes can also create an optional solid residue.\n\nThe tank accepts one liquid type at a time and stores up to 640,000 mB. Drain it before switching between Liquified Aetherium and Dark Matter. The liquid can be extracted through liquid I/O or standard UtilityCraft fluid containers.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Input§r exposes the solid material input.\n§cResidue Output§r exposes the optional byproduct.\n\nLiquid I/O:\n§cLiquid Output§r exposes the produced liquid tank.
ui.utilitycraft:io.liquifier.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Input\n§r- §cResidue Output
ui.utilitycraft:io.liquifier.liquids=I/O Modes:\n§r- §cLiquid Output
ui.utilitycraft:info.residue_processor=Recovers useful materials from residue and other recyclable inputs. Place one supported material in the input slot; the primary result is stored in the upper output, while an optional chance-based residue is stored in the lower output.\n\nEvery input resolves directly to one recipe. Processing speed depends on recipe energy cost, installed upgrades, and the current process batch.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Input§r exposes the material input.\n§cPrimary Output§r exposes the guaranteed result.\n§cResidue Output§r exposes the optional byproduct.\n§cOutput All§r exposes both outputs.
ui.utilitycraft:io.residue_processor.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Input\n§r- §cPrimary Output\n§r- §cResidue Output\n§r- §cOutput All
ui.utilitycraft:info.centrifugal_siever=Processes UtilityCraft sieve recipes through a shared four-slot input pool and a reusable Mesh. Drops are rolled once per processed item and stored in the 15-slot output buffer.\n\nSteam is optional. A boosted cycle consumes 125 units per processed item, runs at 150% rate, and costs 125% energy.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Input§r exposes all material inputs.\n§bMesh§r exposes the mesh slot.\n§cOutput§r exposes the output buffer.\n\nGas I/O:\n§9Steam Input§r accepts Steam.
ui.utilitycraft:io.centrifugal_siever.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Input\n§r- §bMesh\n§r- §cOutput
ui.utilitycraft:io.centrifugal_siever.gases=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Steam Input
ui.utilitycraft:info.dual_siever=Runs two UtilityCraft sieve lanes against one shared 20-slot output buffer. Each lane has one material input and its own reusable Mesh.\n\nIND: each ready lane advances and completes independently.\nSHR: both lanes advance together only when both are ready and contain the same input item.\n\nSteam is optional. A boosted lane consumes 125 units per item, runs at 150% rate, and costs 125% energy. Speed, Energy, Hyper Processing, and Process Batch upgrades are accepted.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Lane A§r and §bLane B§r expose their inputs and meshes.\n§cOutput§r exposes the shared buffer.\n\nGas I/O:\n§9Steam Input§r accepts Steam.
ui.utilitycraft:io.dual_siever.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Lane A Input\n§r- §bLane A Mesh\n§r- §9Lane B Input\n§r- §bLane B Mesh\n§r- §9All Inputs\n§r- §bAll Meshes\n§r- §cOutput
ui.utilitycraft:io.dual_siever.gases=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Steam Input
ui.utilitycraft:info.impact_crusher=Processes two Crusher recipes in parallel into a shared 4x2 output area. Lava heats the machine and fuels each craft; processing begins after the minimum operating temperature is reached. Steam actively dissipates heat. At maximum heat, Thermal Lock stops all processing for at least 30 seconds and releases only after the machine cools below its operating threshold.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Input 1§r and §bInput 2§r feed the two lanes.\n§cOutputs§r expose all eight result slots.\n\nLiquid I/O:\n§vFuel Input§r accepts Lava.\nGas I/O:\n§9Steam Input§r accepts Steam for cooling.
ui.utilitycraft:io.impact_crusher.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Input 1\n§r- §bInput 2\n§r- §9Input All\n§r- §cOutput 1\n§r- §cOutput 2\n§r- §cOutput 3
ui.utilitycraft:io.impact_crusher.liquids=I/O Modes:\n§r- §vLava Input
ui.utilitycraft:info.industrial_burner=Processes three Furnace recipes in parallel. Each lane has one input, one progress bar, and a dedicated 2x1 output buffer. Lava can add up to one bonus craft per base craft, consuming 250 mB for each bonus craft.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Inputs 1-3§r feed their respective lanes.\n§cOutputs 1-3§r each expose two slots.\n§cOutput All§r exposes all six result slots.\n\nLiquid I/O:\n§vFuel Input§r accepts Lava.
ui.utilitycraft:io.industrial_burner.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Input 1\n§r- §bInput 2\n§r- §9Input 3\n§r- §9Input All\n§r- §cOutput 1\n§r- §cOutput 2\n§r- §cOutput 3\n§r- §cOutput All
ui.utilitycraft:io.industrial_burner.liquids=I/O Modes:\n§r- §vFuel Input
ui.utilitycraft:info.arc_press_forge=Processes Electro Press recipes through shared 2x2 input and output buffers.\n\nLow Loss: preserves every output at the normal superior rate.\nHigh Speed: doubles processing rate and batch size, but each completed batch has a 50% chance to lose one output.\n\nSteam optionally adds a further 150% rate boost for 125 units per craft at 125% energy cost.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Input§r exposes the complete input grid.\n§cOutput§r exposes the complete output grid.\n\nGas I/O:\n§9Steam Input§r accepts Steam.
ui.utilitycraft:io.arc_press_forge.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Input\n§r- §cOutput
ui.utilitycraft:info.pulverizer=Processes Crusher recipes through shared 2x2 input and output buffers. All four input slots form one pool, and all four output slots form another.\n\nThe machine runs normally without Steam. When Steam is available, each craft consumes 250 units, processing rate increases to 175%, and energy cost increases to 150%.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Input§r exposes the complete input grid.\n§cOutput§r exposes the complete output grid.\n\nGas I/O:\n§9Steam Input§r accepts Steam.

## Generators
